{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1b217440dacbc54f25b051a141bd391269c41f509d78b4502ada01f572d74bb9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation involves cloning rllab at a specific commit and pip-installing packages such as joblib, theano, keras, tensorflow, gym, tensorflow_probability, and maci."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d95211fe73d3f9ae2202c7c28deade8371c39ef89bc2d6a6134b252e8df1ad3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the repository is not really active due to limited development time, and that breaking changes may occur."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b1b553bd054c3723d0a9cdf15704557f32817f992f35c5189cc3b58b9ab8a36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project requires Python 3.6+, Numpy, Nashpy, and Matplotlib, and additionally depends on the mapr2 module from a separate GitHub repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_61e3202353768dad80642486389778d3d02f0fe28bc34ad4ece26f2726632657"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Default parameter values include grid size 3, gamma 0.95, epsilon 0.5, 1000 iterations, learning rate 0.9, and method 'Q'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7d7c5d511c5d89b5ec67a6a441bfb9a7f2151e17212c1079239ba57b6a01cd22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The program is stated to be checked only for the case of two agents (n_agents=2)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_901eb3f779301a802238c7b77de033a873d1a965e4abe481d16c5c32142f2892"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"DeepGame implements single- and multi-agent learning algorithms, including vanilla Q-learning where each agent behaves optimally per Q-values, and Nash Q-learning aiming for Nash equilibrium."},{"claim_ids":["clm_991f99ad189dc73fce08739833b4136501cf3146af09b80fe527abc4c144ca68"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The learning_rate argument is described as applying to the Q-learning method, and the method argument selects between Q-learning and Nash-Q."},{"claim_ids":["clm_99a7222cf8ffba50f9169124e4bd36934b5325f2c5731dd47b2eb17b887a0fd4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The program is run via run_grid_game.py, configurable through CLI arguments including grid size, gamma, epsilon, iterations, learning rate, and method selection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7c7f04d5d3c938471198771e8587a033e2ed2c87604f5cbcb8f5389d84465f7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README instructs users to run the program with 'python run_grid_game.py' using default parameters, and to adjust hyperparameters via its command-line arguments."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1b217440dacbc54f25b051a141bd391269c41f509d78b4502ada01f572d74bb9","clm_1d95211fe73d3f9ae2202c7c28deade8371c39ef89bc2d6a6134b252e8df1ad3","clm_4b1b553bd054c3723d0a9cdf15704557f32817f992f35c5189cc3b58b9ab8a36","clm_61e3202353768dad80642486389778d3d02f0fe28bc34ad4ece26f2726632657","clm_7d7c5d511c5d89b5ec67a6a441bfb9a7f2151e17212c1079239ba57b6a01cd22","clm_901eb3f779301a802238c7b77de033a873d1a965e4abe481d16c5c32142f2892","clm_991f99ad189dc73fce08739833b4136501cf3146af09b80fe527abc4c144ca68","clm_99a7222cf8ffba50f9169124e4bd36934b5325f2c5731dd47b2eb17b887a0fd4","clm_f7c7f04d5d3c938471198771e8587a033e2ed2c87604f5cbcb8f5389d84465f7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:59:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_36106f2ae1b44160b54b34ca1145cf1e","id":"pg_50f7020866bd53c5ac3ed32fb7fe2264","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ismorphism-deepgame-readme-md-88e6f8927f9c-d32fb7fe2264.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8e463dd36db05cdf955758c0b8807a08"],"title":"ismorphism/DeepGame/README.md @ 88e6f8927f9c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:59:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36106f2ae1b44160b54b34ca1145cf1e"}
